### TITLE ###
BlankLineClosesABlockTheHookWouldKeepOpen
### DESCRIPTION ###
IsComplete never returns true here, so without the blank-line rule the buffer
could not be closed by any keystroke. An indentation-scoped language has no
block terminator, which is why the editor owns this rule rather than the caller.
### PROMPT ###
>
### CONT_PROMPT ###
.
### POLICY ###
never
### KEYS ###
"forever"
enter
enter
### VALUE ###
forever
### OUTCOME ###
submitted
